@Passage-Section Partial hash collision postage scheme
@Passage-Text The idea of using partial hashes is that they can be made arbitrarily expensive to compute (by choosing the desired number of bits of collision), and yet can be verified instantly.
@Passage-Context Back describes the cost-to-create and ease-to-verify property of his Hashcash scheme.
@Passage-JevQuestion Does this passage explain the computational trade-off in the author’s proposed Hashcash scheme?
